GNSS status and NMEA on the callbacks a targetSdk >= 31 app may use.

AndroWish registers these listeners in onCreate whenever location permission
is held, before any veles Tcl runs. For an app targeting API 31 or higher (this
APK targets 36) LocationManager.addGpsStatusListener throws
UnsupportedOperationException ("GpsStatus APIs not supported"), so on any
Android 12+ device with location granted DesktopActivity died at start. The
GpsStatus.NmeaListener overload of addNmeaListener does not throw, but since
Android 11 it registers nothing and returns false, so NMEA never arrived.
Both move to their API 24 replacements (minSdk is 26): GnssStatus.Callback for
start/stop/first-fix/satellites, OnNmeaMessageListener for NMEA sentences.
The hunks are made against the tree after platform-apis.patch.
